        <h2>About the programme</h2>
        <p>Interestring Quartet has always set out to break down the borders between classical music and jazz. Every piece in this concert is an original work that traces the lives of its members: a journey for the ears that blends faraway colours, local feeling and the spirit of improvisation.</p>
        <h2>Performers</h2>
        <dl class="lineup"><div><dt>Violin I</dt><dd>Huang Wei-chun</dd></div><div><dt>Violin II</dt><dd>Huang Hsin-yu</dd></div><div><dt>Viola</dt><dd>Yeh Ti-chi</dd></div><div><dt>Cello</dt><dd>Yeh Chun-lin</dd></div></dl>
        <h2>About the ensemble</h2>
        <p>Interestring Quartet is the first jazz string quartet in the Chinese-speaking world. With jazz at its core, it draws on pop, rock, Latin and folk, and has released three albums of original music.</p>
